If a patient has a multiple-joint-osteoarthritis-pain then every clinician may use a systemic-NSAID for the patient and may use a duloxetine for the patient.
If a patient has an osteoarthritis-pain and a topical-NSAID does not completely control the osteoarthritis-pain then every clinician may use a systemic-NSAID for the patient and may use a duloxetine for the patient.
